        "assertions": [
            "Before authoring the geometry the agent explains the source using a Reading: block, choosing overlay mode with 1.5 seconds per step and a 1.5 second hold, and uses the supplied reference image instead of generating a replacement diagram.",
            "The delivered spec has background.image resolving to a companion image beside the spec, canvas 960x540, and four invisible type: anchor nodes at the supplied bounds. The original image bytes are copied, with no redrawn title, boxes, text or icons and no visible static paths.",
            "All three explicit edge point lists follow the supplied coordinates with exact corners (default radius 0 in overlay mode, or explicit 0). animation.steps first travels client-to-API, then both fan-out edges together, with trail false. The original arrows are neither replaced nor rounded.",
            "The initializer, lint and renderer were used, the render included --format mp4 --verify --check, and background_pixels_preserved plus background_file_unchanged both passed in the renderer report. The reply reports the 4.5-second duration and names the video, PNG, editable spec and companion background.",
            "The reply explains that MP4 needs the player's repeat setting to loop. It does not falsely claim visual inspection if no image-viewing tool was available, and in that case states that the supplied coordinates were used."
